UPDATE companies SET description='FAT ENZO, Inc. operates from Monroe, Connecticut, where it was founded in January 2009 as a family-owned and operated garment decoration shop. The company was incorporated by four partners: Robert Vincent Piccirillo (CEO), Matthew Anthony Piazza (CCO, deceased 2019), Joan Karen Iannotti (CFO, deceased 2021), and their canine mascot Enzo Piccirillo, who inspired the brand name and logo.

The shop specializes in custom screen printing, embroidery, and graphic design, handling all decoration in-house on apparel including t-shirts, caps, totes, polos, hoodies, and uniforms. An internal art department provides illustration, logo creation, color separation, vectorization, and digitization, while additional services span copywriting, brand development, online retailing, fulfillment, and drop-shipping.

FAT ENZO serves a broad client base across the Northeast (Connecticut, Vermont, Rhode Island, Massachusetts, New York, New Jersey) and Florida, with a focus on three core segments: touring bands and musicians, streetwear and lifestyle brands requiring contract printing and fulfillment, and businesses needing uniforms or promotional wear. The company also works with political campaigns, sports teams, motorcycle clubs, college organizations, religious groups, and non-profits.

The company emphasizes domestic production under its motto "MADE IN A SWEATSHOP IN THE U.S.A.," stating that no work is outsourced overseas. It positions itself as a creative brigade offering grammatically correct, obsessively detailed artwork and unorthodox marketing, with rush delivery available for time-sensitive orders.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom screen printing", "Embroidery", "Graphic design", "Illustration", "Custom logo creation", "Color separation", "Vectorization", "Digitization", "Copywriting/creative concepts", "Brand development", "Online retailing/fulfillment", "Rush delivery", "Contract screen printing", "Garment tagging and bagging", "Drop-shipping", "Custom apparel decoration (t-shirts, caps, totes, polos, hoodies, uniforms)"], "industries": ["Music bands and touring acts", "Streetwear and lifestyle brands", "Businesses (uniforms, promotional)", "Political organizations and campaigns", "Sports teams (including bowling, darts, roller derby)", "Motorcycle clubs", "College fraternities and sororities", "Religious organizations", "Social clubs", "Non-profit organizations", "Corporations", "Mom-and-pop shops"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All production kept in-house in the U.S. with no overseas outsourcing", "In-house art department handling design, illustration, color separation, and digitization", "Contract screen printing with tagging, bagging, and nationwide drop-ship fulfillment", "Rush delivery offered for urgent orders", "Family-owned operation emphasizing bold, unorthodox creative work"], "facts_used": ["Founded January 2009 -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /about, /", "Headquarters at 600 Main Street, Unit D, Monroe, CT 06468 -> /about, /", "Founders: Robert Vincent Piccirillo (CEO), Matthew Anthony Piazza (CCO), Joan Karen Iannotti (CFO), Enzo Piccirillo (mascot) -> /about", "Services: custom screen printing, embroidery, graphic design, illustration, logo creation, color separation, vectorization, digitization, copywriting, brand development, online retailing/fulfillment, rush delivery -> /services, /about", "Products: t-shirts, caps, totes, polos, hoodies, uniforms -> /about, /", "Industries served: bands, brands, businesses, political organizations, sports teams, motorcycle clubs, college fraternities/sororities, religious groups, social clubs, non-profits, corporations, mom-and-pop shops -> /about", "Motto: MADE IN A SWEATSHOP IN THE U.S.A. -> /about, /", "No overseas outsourcing -> /services", "Contract screen printing with tagging, bagging, drop-ship fulfillment -> /services, /about", "Serves Northeast (CT, VT, RI, MA, NY, NJ) and Florida -> /about, /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "FAT ENZO is a Family-Owned & Operated SweatShop now based in Monroe, Connecticut... We specialize in high-quality Custom Screen Printing, Embroidery, and Graphic Design... Everything is customized in-house: T-SHIRTS, CAPS, TOTES, POLOS, HOODIES, UNIFORMS.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fat-enzo-t-shirts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='FBK Medical Tubing, Inc. was founded in 1981 in Georgetown, Delaware. The company operates as part of D&B Industrial Group, though the founding individuals are not named in public materials. From its start, the business focused on precision thermoplastic extrusion for medical applications.

The company extrudes a range of medical tubing configurations including multi-lumen, single lumen, profile, colored, and co-extruded multi-layer profiles. Beyond extrusion, FBK provides extensive post-extrusion finishing services such as tip and radius forming, cut and flare, thermoforming, punch and skive, printing and imaging, balloon installation, tipping and sealing, and support beading. These capabilities allow the firm to deliver sub-assemblies or finished components from a single source. Materials processed include various thermoplastics and polyurethane.

FBK serves the medical device industry, supplying disposable medical products to a diverse customer base. Its product development team works with clients on prototype evaluation and complex multi-lumen profile design, though specific customer names are not disclosed.

The company states its operating rule is to ship high-quality products on time and within budget. It emphasizes its particular adeptness at designing and producing complex multi-lumen profiles and offers a dedicated product development team for prototype evaluation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Multi-lumen extrusion", "Single lumen extrusion", "Profile tubing extrusion", "Colored tubing extrusion", "Co-extrusion (multi-layer)", "Tip and radius forming", "Cut and flare", "Thermoforming", "Punch and skive", "Printing and imaging", "Balloon installation", "Prototyping", "Tipping and sealing", "Support beading"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Disposable medical products"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics", "Polyurethane"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Ship high-quality products on time and within budget", "Adept at designing and producing complex multi-lumen profiles", "Extensive post-extrusion finishing services for single-source sub-assemblies", "Product development team for prototype evaluation"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1981 -> /", "Headquarters in Georgetown, Delaware -> /", "Manufactures precision thermoplastic medical tubing -> /", "Offers multi-lumen, single lumen, profile, colored, co-extrusion processes -> /", "Provides post-extrusion finishing: tip and radius, cut and flare, thermoform, punch and skive, print/image, balloon installation, tipping and sealing, support beading -> /", "Materials: thermoplastics, polyurethane -> /", "Serves medical device industry, disposable medical products -> /", "Product development team for prototypes and complex multi-lumen profiles -> /", "Operating rule: ship high-quality products on time and within budget -> /", "Part of D&B Industrial Group (copyright) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "FBK Medical Tubing, Inc. manufactures and fabricates precision thermoplastic, medical tubing", "foun