UPDATE companies SET description='Factory Furniture Company has operated from Mauldin, South Carolina since 1964, when the Kern family opened the business to help Upstate residents furnish their homes without the markup of big-box retailers. The company remains family-owned and operated today.

The retailer carries furniture from more than 34 manufacturers, offering over 10,000 items across bedroom, living room, dining, home office, and outdoor categories. Rather than holding inventory, the team places orders directly with the manufacturer and coordinates delivery to the customer''s door. Financing is available through a lending partner.

The showroom serves residential customers throughout the Upstate region. Shoppers can browse brands online or in person, then request a quote for specific SKUs or descriptions. The staff, described as non-commissioned product experts, assist with selection and pricing.

The business was founded on the premise that direct manufacturer relationships allow lower prices than traditional retail. The company emphasizes that customers speak with knowledgeable staff rather than commissioned salespeople, and that the ordering process is streamlined into three steps: browse, reach out, and let the company handle the rest.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture retail sales", "Direct manufacturer ordering", "Delivery coordination", "Financing facilitation", "Product sourcing across 34+ brands"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings", "Home office furniture", "Outdoor furniture"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Typically responds within one business day for quotes", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1964", "Direct relationships with 34+ furniture manufacturers", "Factory-direct pricing by ordering straight from manufacturers", "Non-commissioned product experts assist customers", "Financing available through lending partner"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1964 -> db", "Headquarters Mauldin, SC -> db", "Family-owned (Kern family) -> /", "34+ manufacturers carried -> /", "10,000+ items available -> /", "50+ years in business -> /", "Direct manufacturer ordering and delivery coordination -> /", "Financing through lending partner -> /", "Showroom at 729 N. Main St. Mauldin, SC -> /", "Categories: Bedroom, Living Room, Dining, Home Office, Outdoor/Patio -> /", "Responds within one business day -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We carry dozens of name-brand manufacturers and pass our savings straight to you.", "founded_year": "1964", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='factory-furniture-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Factory Motor Parts (FMP) traces its roots to 1945 when Elliott Auto Supply Co., Inc. opened a single location in Minneapolis. The business was later renamed Factory Motor Parts through its involvement in the Chrysler Mopar distribution network of the 1960s, forging partnerships with Ford, General Motors and other aftermarket suppliers. Today the company is headquartered in Eagan, Minnesota, and operates as a multi‑generational, family‑owned enterprise with more than 300 locations across 35 states.

FMP functions as a full‑line automotive aftermarket distributor, supplying original‑equipment (OE) and name‑brand parts to professional repair shops. Its catalog is backed by dedicated support teams, an online ordering platform (FMP Delivers), fleet supply‑chain solutions, GPS tracking, training programs and a customer self‑service portal. Specialized offerings include a Professional Brake Program, Battery Programs, a Stocking Program, the FMP Partners Network for independent shops, and a One Stop Parts Source Program.

The distributor serves independent service centers, car and truck dealerships, commercial fleets, wholesale distributors and automotive retailers. Testimonials on the site cite customers such as Christian Brothers Automotive, Tilden Car Care Center and Colorado Tire & Service as examples of shops that rely on FMP for parts availability and warranty support.

