UPDATE companies SET description='Falcon Plastics was founded in 1975 in Brookings, South Dakota, as a family-owned operation molding customer ideas into plastic products. Over nearly five decades, the company has grown from its Midwestern roots into a multi-facility contract molder with plants in South Dakota, Oregon, and Tennessee, supplemented by strategic manufacturing partnerships in Mexico and Asia.

The company specializes in mid-to-high volume custom injection molding, blow molding, tool and mold making, sheet foaming (EVA), and foam-in-place gasketing. Its facilities employ smart work cells equipped with process monitoring, automated in-line quality testing, and robotic part acceptance/rejection systems, all governed by lean manufacturing principles. Dedicated white rooms with HEPA filtration support cleanroom molding requirements, while value-added assembly and full program management extend services beyond the press.

Falcon serves medical device, electronics, consumer product, and automotive OEMs, along with customers in consumer health aids, business machines, construction, and recreation/sports. The firm produces precision components that meet strict regulatory standards for medical applications, durable housings for electronics, and high-performance parts for automotive systems.

The company emphasizes a multi-facility model that provides supply-chain flexibility without sacrificing control or quality. Its stated differentiators include cycle-time reduction, material optimization, competitive pricing, and an ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system driven by continuous improvement and on-time delivery. The family-owned legacy underscores a culture of long-term partnership and customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom injection molding", "Custom blow molding", "Tool and mold making", "Sheet foaming (EVA)", "Foam-in-place gasketing", "Value-added assembly", "Full program management", "Process monitoring", "Automated in-line quality testing", "Robotic part acceptance/rejection", "Lean manufacturing", "Cleanroom molding (white rooms with HEPA filtration)", "Quality assurance (ISO 9001:2015)", "Supply chain management (multi-facility)"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Electronics", "Consumer Products", "Automotive", "Consumer Health Aids", "Business Machines", "Construction", "Recreation/Sports"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Smart work cells with process monitoring systems", "Automated in-line quality testing systems", "Robotic acceptance/rejection systems", "HEPA air filtration systems", "Precision molds"], "volume": "Mid-to-high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multi-facility model with U.S., Mexico, and Asia manufacturing locations", "Smart work cells with process monitoring and automated in-line quality testing", "White rooms with HEPA filtration for cleanroom molding", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Family-owned with five decades of U.S.-based precision molding expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 in Brookings, SD -> /about", "Family-owned -> / (homepage)", "Facilities in South Dakota, Oregon, Tennessee -> /quality", "Strategic manufacturing in Mexico and Asia -> / (homepage)", "Mid-to-high volume custom plastic molder 