UPDATE companies SET description='Fashions Unlimited was founded in 1976 by Phil Spector in Baltimore, Maryland. After a decade working for a local manufacturer, Spector opened the facility to provide full-service apparel production. The company remains a domestic manufacturing operation in Baltimore.

The shop specializes in activewear, intimate apparel, and swimwear constructed from stretch fabrics. Services span product development, pattern making and grading using AccuMark software, 3D digital rendering, cutting and sewing on overlock, single-needle lockstitch, coverstitch, zig‑zag, and flatlock machines, and a Gerber automatic cutter for precision. Finishing includes tagging, bagging, and bulk shipping; repair work covers retagging and rebagging. Production minimums start at 200 pieces per style, with a typical initial order of 300 pieces across multiple colors and sizes.

Clients range from emerging brands to established labels in the activewear, intimate apparel, and swimwear sectors. The company also serves medical‑apparel customers such as Miss Daisy Medical. Fashions Unlimited does not handle tailored wovens, denim, sequins, or silk, and sources all materials domestically.

The firm emphasizes its status as one of the few remaining onshore apparel factories, marketing “Made in the USA” output. Differentiators include in‑house 3D rendering (rare in Maryland), digital pattern workflows that reduce sample iterations, and Spector’s 50‑plus years of industry experience guiding development and costing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product development", "Pattern making (AccuMark)", "3D digital rendering (AccuMark)", "Cutting & sewing (stretch fabrics)", "Automatic cutting (Gerber)", "Finishing (tagging, bagging, bulk shipping)", "Repair work (retagging, rebagging)", "Consultation", "Material sourcing (domestic only)"], "industries": ["Activewear", "Intimate apparel", "Swimwear", "Medical apparel"], "materials": ["Stretch fabrics", "Rubber/elastic", "Bra cups", "Hardware", "Sew-in labels", "Heat transfers"], "equipment": ["Overlock machines", "Single-needle lockstitch machines", "Coverstitch machines", "Zig-zag machines", "Flatlock machines", "Gerber automatic cutting machine", "AccuMark pattern software", "AccuMark 3D rendering software"], "volume": "Prototype to 200+ pieces per style", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the few remaining onshore apparel manufacturing facilities in the U.S.", "In\u2011house 3D digital rendering via AccuMark (rare in Maryland)", "Gerber automatic cutting for higher accuracy than manual cutting", "Specialized stretch\u2011fabric machinery (overlock, coverstitch, flatlock, etc.)", "Transparent hourly development billing with 50% deposit to start"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 by Phil Spector -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Baltimore, Maryland -> /about-us", "Specializes in activewear, intimate apparel, swimwear with stretch fabrics -> /about-us", "Services: product development, pattern making, 3D rendering, cutting & sewing, finishing, repair -> /about-us", "Machines: overlock, single-needle lockstitch, coverstitch, zig-zag, flatlock, Gerber automatic cutter