UPDATE companies SET description='Fernwood Designs Woodworking operates from a shop in Mars Hill, North Carolina, nestled in the Blue Ridge Mountains of western North Carolina. The business was founded by Rich Grenier, who serves as owner and creator, and runs the operation from a property he shares with his wife, artist Francine D’Antuono. A wooded path connects their home to the workshop, providing daily inspiration for his work.

The shop produces a range of custom wood products and milling services. Offerings include custom cabinetry, furniture spanning farmhouse rustic to refined urban styles, wood countertops and table tops, built-in units, tongue-and-groove milling for flooring and ceilings, lathe-turned legs and trim, and milling and sanding of raw lumber up to 50 inches wide. The company also provides epoxy and stone inlays, fine art frames, interior and exterior doors, trim, and mouldings, along with design services that deliver detailed drawings and plans for projects of any scale.

The company’s project portfolio includes kitchens, individual furniture pieces, and architectural millwork for both interior and exterior applications.

Grenier emphasizes the artistic qualities of wood, working with exotic species and reclaimed boards salvaged from old structures. He treats each piece as a unique work of art, preserving the wood’s natural character through assembly. The addition of design services, led by D’Antuono, allows clients to visualize projects before fabrication begins.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry", "Furniture manufacturing (farmhouse rustic to refined urban)", "Wood countertop and table top fabrication", "Custom built-in units", "Tongue-and-groove milling for flooring and ceilings", "Lathe turning for legs and trim", "Milling and sanding of raw lumber up to 50 inches wide", "Epoxy and stone inlay", "Fine art frame making", "Interior and exterior door manufacturing", "Trim and moulding production", "Design and drafting services"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Exotic lumber", "Reclaimed lumber", "Various wood species", "Epoxy", "Stone"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Works with exotic and reclaimed lumber sourced from historic structures", "Each piece of wood treated as an individual work of art", "In-house design services with detailed drawings and plans", "Milling and sanding capacity for raw lumber up to 50 inches wide", "Epoxy and stone inlay capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Location: Mars Hill, NC -> db", "Owner: Rich Grenier -> /about-us", "Wife/artist: Francine D''Antuono -> /about-us", "Shop on peaceful parcel with wooded path -> /about-us", "Services: custom cabinetry, furniture, countertops, built-ins, tongue-and-groove milling, lathe turning, milling/sanding up to 50\" wide, epoxy/stone inlays, fine art frames, doors, trim/mouldings -> /about-us", "Design services offered with detailed drawings -> /about-us", "Works with exotic and reclaimed lumber -> /about-us", "Artistic approach to wood selection and assembly -> /about-us", "Phone number  -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The shop is fully equipped to handle all kinds of projects including: Custom Cabinetry, Furniture from Farmhouse Rustic to Refined Urban, Wood Counter/Table Tops, Custom Built In Units, Tongue & Groove Milling for Flooring & Ceilings, Lathe Turned Table Legs and Trimmings, Milling/Sanding for Raw Lumber up to 50\" Wide, Epoxy & Stone Inlays, Fine Art Frames, Door/ Interior and Exterior, Trims and Mouldings", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fernwood-designs-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ferraro Foods traces its roots to 1975, when founder Ferraro established the business in Greenbrook, New Jersey. The company later relocated its headquarters to Mebane, North Carolina, where it operates today as an Italian specialty food distributor.

The distributor carries thousands of stock-keeping units spanning pasta, premium cheeses, tomatoes, flour, beverages, meats, seafood, appetizers, desserts, and packaging such as pizza boxes and food containers. Its logistics network relies on multi-temperature trucks and refrigerated loading docks to maintain product integrity across a footprint that serves more than 8,000 customers in 26 states.

Ferraro Foods targets the foodservice sector, supplying restaurants, pizzerias, caterers, and other operators that require consistent access to Italian and specialty ingredients. The company’s online ordering platform and monthly product publication, FRESCO by Ferraro, are designed to keep buyers current with new items and seasonal trends.

