, "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-bank-of-delaware' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Physics was founded in 2012 in Boise, Idaho, and operates from facilities in Boise and Chelmsford, Essex, United Kingdom. The company was established to identify and maximize the potential of new technologies in the food and beverage industry.

The firm provides Pulsed Electric Field (PEF) systems for food processing as the sole North American, UK, and Irish distributor for Elea, the German manufacturer of the equipment. Food Physics customizes each PEF system to a client’s production line, offers pilot-scale testing at its partner facilities in the United States, Britain, and Germany, and supports installations with a spare-parts dispatch and field-service team. More than 100 PEF systems have been installed globally.

Customers span food and beverage processing, agricultural processing, and scientific research. Applications include potato-chip and french-fry production, freeze-drying, vegetable and fruit processing, winemaking, spirulina extraction for food and textile dyes, and dried-produce improvement. The company serves clients of all sizes across North America, the United Kingdom, and Ireland.

Food Physics emphasizes innovation, with over 17 PEF-related patents pending and collaborative R&D projects that drive new commercial applications. Its mission is to deliver systems that increase yield, improve product stability, and reduce waste, enabling products from freeze-dried foods to paints to reach the market efficiently.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pulsed Electric Field (PEF) system integration and customization", "PEF pilot-scale testing and trial batch processing", "Food processing research and development", "Spare parts supply and logistics", "Field service, maintenance, and on-site training", "Custom PEF system design for production lines", "Collaborative R&D project management"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Beverage processing", "Agricultural processing", "Food technology research and development", "Scientific research"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Elea Pulsed Electric Field systems", "PEF Pilot trial batch system", "Belt Advantage system (tubers, roots, vegetables, fruits)", "Pipe Advantage system (liquid foods, non-foods, wastewater)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["More than 100 PEF systems installed globally", "Sole provider of Elea PEF systems in North America, UK, and Ireland", "Pilot hall facilities in the United States, Britain, and Germany", "Over 17 PEF-related patents pending", "Spare-parts dispatch for rapid service response"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2012 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Boise, Idaho and Chelmsford, Essex, UK -> /about-us", "Sole provider of Elea PEF systems in North America, UK, Ireland -> /", "More than 100 PEF systems installed globally -> /", "Pilot hall facilities in America, Britain, Germany -> /", "Over 17 PEF-related patents pending -> /", "Spare-parts dispatch for quick delivery -> /", "Team members: Kalen McKenzie (Partner/CEO), Riley Gomez (Operations Manager), David Lethcoe (Field Service Manager), Rylan McKenzie (Finance Manager)